@@ -2,6 +2,25 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## SMS sign-up verification
+
+Set the server-only environment variables in `.env.example` using a Twilio account
+and Verify Service. Configure the service for **6-digit codes** with a **10-minute
+validity period**, and enable its domain-bound SMS option with the deployed
+website hostname. The SMS must end with `@your-hostname #123456` (using the actual
+code) for WebOTP and compatible device autofill. See
+[Twilio Verify](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/api) and the
+[browser SMS format requirements](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/web-apis/web-otp).
+Production requires HTTPS. No credentials or OTPs are returned to the browser.
+
+The sign-up route sends and checks codes on the server, ties the challenge to the
+current session and phone number, limits retries, and calls the existing
+registration service only after verification succeeds. Configure Twilio Verify
+fraud protection and service rate limits for production traffic. The external
+registration service must also restrict direct registration if verification is
+to be mandatory for clients outside this app; that service is not in this repo.
+Astro sessions must use shared persistent storage when running multiple instances.
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
